implementationPlan.description:
Regression check, run once and fresh from the repo root. This is the DoD command `cd packages/moe-proxy && npm test`, run inside a Linux snapshot. The shared checkout's packages/moe-proxy/node_modules is a Windows install: from WSL, npm test there deletes dist and then fails tsc (Serena memory gotcha-proxy-npm-test-shared-checkout-deletes-dist).
Command: `bash -c 'set -e; SNAP=$(mktemp -d); git archive HEAD packages/moe-proxy | tar -x -C "$SNAP"; cp packages/moe-proxy/src/utils.ts packages/moe-proxy/src/utils.test.ts "$SNAP/packages/moe-proxy/src/"; cd "$SNAP/packages/moe-proxy"; npm ci --no-audit --no-fund; env -i HOME="$HOME" PATH="$(dirname "$(command -v node)"):/usr/bin:/bin" TMPDIR=/tmp npm test'`
It must exit 0, with the pretest tsc build passing and every test green. A plan-time dry run on HEAD passed 84/84 in about 24 s. On a native Windows seat, the same recipe in Git Bash works. This command's fresh output is the moe.complete_task verification evidence; name the snapshot path in the summary.
Then run a quick mutation proof on a copy of the snapshot. Apply each mutation alone, run vitest on src/utils.test.ts, confirm it fails, then restore:
M1 drop complete_step from the table;
M2 drop complete_task;
M3 give the completion tools only ['session'];
M4 register only the moe.x spelling for them.
Record the failing test names in the step note.
